WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.769 line:0%
Welcome back to another episode
of the<i> Wine Down.</i>

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.971 line:0%
Today we are joined
by Alexander Hodge,

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:08.074
who plays Molly's love interest,
Andrew,

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.142
to discuss "Lowkey Trippin'."

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:13.146
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:18.218
This was a big episode
for Andrew and Molly.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.018
Yeah.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.554
What do you think this trip
says about their relationship?

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.856
I mean I don't think
Andrew and Molly, uh,

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.459 line:0%
I don't think they take
family lightly, either of them.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.694 line:0%
So the fact that
somebody's meeting

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.363
someone else's family,
is like,

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.898
things are getting pretty--
pretty serious

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:32.966
between these two.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.500
Can you talk about
Andrew's journey?

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.537
Ooh. Yeah, I think Andrew--
Andrew's been confronted,

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.572
I think, for the first time,
Andrew's sort of been

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.275
really challenged
by a strong personality

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.243
in a relationship.
So this is the first time

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:47.079
where he's been like,
"Oh, okay. I need to contribute

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.148
in some way
that makes me uncomfortable."

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:51.951
And so I think mainly
that's been being vulnerable,

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.286
and opening up, and like,
you know,

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:57.190
just being an Asian man,
and being raised

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.759
the way he was,
talking about things

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.228
that don't make him feel strong
or make him feel insecure,

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.429
are really difficult for him.

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:05.464 line:0%
What do you think, sort of,
is going through Molly's head,

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:07.200 line:0%
uh, during her argument
with Victor,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.802 line:0%
about her overreacting
to the towel lady?

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.571
(SIGHS) It's--
I think it's the first time

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:16.275
that Molly's had
to defend her existence

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.078
to somebody who is
of Andrew's side

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:21.514
of the relationship.
So it's like the first time

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:26.051
that Molly's had to explain
what being black is like

00:01:26.151 --> 00:01:29.054
to Victor.
And Andrew is kind of

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:30.924
on the side,
but also at the same time,

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.292
is-- is just trying
to understand

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.194
where both sides
are coming from.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:38.031
And I think in that moment,
what he was trying to do,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.799
by trying to diffuse
the situation,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.168
wasn't actually helpful
because he actually

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.769
made Molly feel more isolated.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.239
This is our first episode
out of the country.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.272
What was it like?

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.342
I think it was--
it infused, I think,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.844
a new energy into the show
to also take a show

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:53.612
that on-paper is about,
you know,

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.849
these two black women that
live in a very specific part

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.883
of L.A.,
and take them and put them--

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.051
and to see why people travel.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.086
-Yeah.
-And to take the show

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.221
and not just show, you know,
obviously, us filming there,

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.023
it's one thing
to see black people, you know,

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.259
in front of the camera,
behind the camera.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.361
Out of the country, you know,
filming a television show.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:11.163
But I think, also,
it does a lot even on screen

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:12.498
to see that,
'cause we do travel.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:15.034
No Issa.
I mean how was that for you

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:16.069
on your side?

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.369
It was a blessing.
I've been waiting

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:19.338
for this moment
for four seasons.

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:20.940
ALEXANDER: She said
let's get three more.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.275
And it was-- Yes,
let's get three.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.742
Next season, woo.

00:02:23.842 --> 00:02:26.278
-I'm not gonna be in none of it.
-Not gonna be in<i> none</i> of it.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:29.916
But I do want to talk about
just the presence

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.317
that Issa has on this trip.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.719
Um... (CHUCKLES)
So I think,

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:37.222
even though Issa was not
appearing in this episode,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.492
Issa definitely featured
heavily.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.560
I feel like it's affected Molly
so much

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.098
because Issa and Molly
are just such a strong presence

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.266
in each other's lives.

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:49.334
I do wonder if the fight
with Issa hadn't happened,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.070
and if she didn't have
that burden on her trip,

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:55.007
if she would have gone so hard
on Victor.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.142
Victor was being a bit
of a dick.

00:02:57.242 --> 00:02:58.778
Mm-hmm, Victor was a dick
for sure.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:02:59.779
Yeah.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.682
I think Victor was the victim
of displacement of her anger.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.417
And I think that's
what's interesting

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.853
about episode six and seven.
Even though they're not

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:10.690
in each other's episodes,
their presence is felt.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.558
That's how strong
these two women are

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:13.893
in each other's lives.
And how much,

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.862
by them not dealing with it,
it's still a presence

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.330
they have to face
in some way.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.299
And so I think that's
what's great about the end

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:21.967
when Yvonne is like,
"I have to sort of

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.202
start to deal with this."

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:25.438
When do you feel like
it's right to react...

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:26.973
or to let it go?

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.175
Speaking as myself,
or what I would like myself

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.211
-to do?
-Speaking as yourself.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.546
-React.
-React all day?

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.048
So the towel--
From the towel lady

00:03:36.448 --> 00:03:39.284
-to the fight in the jacuzzi.
-Yeah.

00:03:39.384 --> 00:03:40.853
-Those are your moves.
-Well I need to--

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.556
I need to work on it.
I'm actively working on this...

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.357
myself.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.691
Doctor Rhonda is available.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:48.027
It is-- Look, I have my own
Doctor Rhonda,

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.696
and she helps me-- I--
I react a lot.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.765
I feel like reacting
might not be the issue.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.935
Overreacting is an issue.
Reacting is not an issue.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.271
But I think when you react,
it's important

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:03.175
to like find a way
to maintain capacity to listen.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.679
Okay, well we can't thank you
enough for joining us this week.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:09.315
Be sure to join us next week
for a new episode

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.883
of the<i> Wine Down.</i>

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.552
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:15.989 line:0%
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

